bench_*
# ...but the published report and the matrix it was computed from are EVIDENCE, not scratch.
# bench_report.py's central claim is that every figure is a pure function of the matrix; that claim
# is only checkable by someone who has the matrix. Keeping the report and dropping its inputs would
# republish exactly the unverifiable-number problem this pipeline was built to remove.
!bench_report_v3.md
!bench_report_v3_real.md
!bench_matrix.jsonl
compare_*
abc
abc.*
test*
verify_*
# The ablation's counterfactuals are DERIVED from logged candidate sizes. This log is the run that
# confronted them with reality (family actually masked off, real archive re-measured, 102/102
# agree). Keeping the claim and discarding its confirmation is how a prediction quietly becomes
# quoted as a measurement.
!verify_grid.log
!verify_filter.log
!verify_numeric.log
!ab_zstd.log
rand_*
repro_*
trace_*
opt_*
simple_*
multi_*
minimal_*
partial_*
real_*
greedy_*
encoder_*
ref_*
output*
nul
python_ref

# Directories
benchmark_data/
alp_sota/
test_files/
ziptest/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVATE WORKING DOCS — this repository is PUBLIC.
#
# internal/ holds the development record (design notes, defect inventories, compliance audits,
# roadmaps). Fifteen of those documents were once committed here by accident and had to be PURGED
# FROM PUBLIC HISTORY. After that they were protected by .git/info/exclude — which is per-clone and
# is NEVER pushed, so the protection existed on exactly one machine and any other clone had none.
# That is the same shape as the original accident. The rule belongs somewhere that travels with the
# repository, so it lives here.
#
# Listing the directory name publicly is the intended trade: a visible ignore rule is much cheaper
# than a second leak. Nothing about the CONTENTS is disclosed by the name.
internal/
/CLAUDE.md

# Python scripts (experimental)
*.py
__pycache__/
# ...but amalgamate.py GENERATES the tracked mzip_amalgamated.hpp; excluding it made the
# shipped single header unreproducible from a fresh clone. (2026-08-12)
!amalgamate.py
# The measurement pipeline: corpus (data) -> bench_run (measure) -> bench_report (report).
# All four are load-bearing; the blanket *.py above would swallow them silently, which is the
# failure check_tracked_deps.sh exists to make visible.
!bench_core.py
!bench_corpus.py
!bench_run.py
!bench_report.py
# Phase 1b: candidate-family ablation. Reads MZCAND telemetry, computes leave-one-family-out, and
# emits CompressionReceipt sidecars.
!family_ablation.py
# but DO track the README/bench helpers
!generate_readme_tables.py
!summarize_real_bench.py

